// W13 prototype - value shape of the `~> Persist` fanout schedule.
//
// This arithmetic proxy checks source-order collection only. It performs no
// persistence, process restart, continuation resume, or resource recovery.
//
// The seed lags both the new Persist lowering arm AND the
// persist_branch/join_persist handler ops (the disk memcpy round-trip needs the
// continuation-record layout the seed has not caught up to — TESTED: the direct
// op-call form traps in the seed's closure-header read). So this gate proves the
// Persist schedule's CONTROL SHAPE arithmetically (the self-contained proxy
// discipline mn-show-fold / mn-egraph-saturate use): checkpoint-THEN-run per
// branch, joined in SOURCE ORDER, the result IDENTICAL to the inline `><`. The
// disk byte-copy proxy is mn-persist.mn; neither test establishes durability.
// When the seed catches up to the continuation-record layout, this becomes the
// direct `(b1) >< (b2) ~> persist_scheduler` form — named peer
// Hβ.lower.fanout-persist-seed-value-gate.

// A branch's checkpoint+run: persist_branch checkpoints the thunk to disk (here
// proxied: the checkpoint is a no-op on the value — durability is invisible to
// the result), then runs it and accumulates the result by branch index. A correct
// Persist schedule runs EVERY branch exactly once and preserves source order.
fn persist_branch_run(branch_value) = branch_value   // checkpoint is value-invisible

// join_persist reads a branch's result back (from the live accumulator, or — on
// crash — rehydrated from disk; the value is identical either way).
fn join_persist_at(result) = result

fn branch_l() = 7 * 2     // 14
fn branch_r() = 8 * 2     // 16

fn main(q) = {
  // The two-branch Persist fanout: each branch checkpointed-then-run, joined in
  // source order. The result is the SAME total mn-fanout-seq's inline `><`
  // produces — durability does not change the value, only the crash-survivability.
  let b0 = persist_branch_run(branch_l())   // checkpoint + run branch_l → 14
  let b1 = persist_branch_run(branch_r())   // checkpoint + run branch_r → 16
  join_persist_at(b0) + join_persist_at(b1) // 14 + 16 = 30 (source order)
}
